  "security_implications": "The block decodes kmac_cmd to drive SHA-3 start/run/done and message-FIFO processing. A malformed or fault-injected kmac_cmd value that falls outside the defined enumeration is silently ignored (no operation asserted). If kmac_cmd originates from a trusted hardware FSM, this fallback may mask a fault that leaves the cryptographic datapath in an unsafe state without alerting. The multi-bit sha3_done_d signal uses MuBi4 encoding for integrity, but the block itself does not verify the integrity of the command input; it relies on upstream correctness. Any compromise of kmac_cmd could directly activate or stall SHA-3 operations, affecting data confidentiality/integrity if keys or digests are involved.",
